\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Pass rates on the HumanEval random-span infilling benchmark~\citep  {bavarian2022fim} with CodeLlama-7b. Left: greedy and pass@10 for the PSM and SPM prompt formats, with token healing~\citep  {dagan2024tokenizer} and token alignment~\citep  {athiwaratkun2024alignment} as baselines (pass@10 is the maximum over the temperature sweep). Right: pass@10 as a function of sampling temperature for byte-level (ours) and token-level predictions. The SPM format forces predictions from the middle of a token, which byte-level predictions handle successfully.}}{9}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fim}{{6}{9}{Pass rates on the HumanEval random-span infilling benchmark~\citep {bavarian2022fim} with CodeLlama-7b. Left: greedy and pass@10 for the PSM and SPM prompt formats, with token healing~\citep {dagan2024tokenizer} and token alignment~\citep {athiwaratkun2024alignment} as baselines (pass@10 is the maximum over the temperature sweep). Right: pass@10 as a function of sampling temperature for byte-level (ours) and token-level predictions. The SPM format forces predictions from the middle of a token, which byte-level predictions handle successfully}{figure.6}{}}
